Well, I suppose this is the theory. Let me reformulate my question.
Presuming that higher enchantments are ranging from rare to extremely
rare, I assume you don't wait until you get +3/+5/+10 arrows. I also
assume you will watch the timeout and constantly produce new arrows
whenever possible or sufficiently likely to succeed. Do you then wait
until you have a stack to enchant? Do you collect arrows of different
enchantments to cancel them and enchant a larger stack? I suppose you
don't waste scrolls of enchant armor on small arrow stacks, do you?

I am asking all this because when I tried it, I mostly get a stack
not too large of +0 arrows. And scrolls of enchant weapons are not
always available in sufficient amounts. But I want them with a high
enchantment. In my ranger games it seems not worthwhile to do that
procedure; it seems easier to train with some daggers (and they seem
to do even more damage than the arrows, as someone showed recently).

Another viable option to get arrows much earlier than from the quest
artifact is to #untrap arrow traps, or get the arrows from the mines'
inhabitants. With those resources there's even less need to wait for
arrows from Diana's bow, and to wait for the timeout.

To summarise; #invoking Diana's bow seems not overly useful to me,
given how it's implemented and given all the alternatives. YMMV.

